<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Topic//EN" "topic.dtd">
<topic id="git-addon-git-staging-view-interface">
  <title>Git Staging View</title>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Git Client add-on<indexterm>Git Staging view</indexterm></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body>
    <p id="p_pbt_wn5_nsb">The <uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol> view is the main interface for
      reviewing changes, staging files, writing commit messages, committing, pushing, and pulling. </p>
    <section id="section_git_staging_how_to_open"><title>Open Git Staging</title><p>To open the
          <uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol> view, on the <ph keyref="product"/> toolbar, go to any
        of the following:</p><ul id="ul_mvd_crq_pjc">
        <li><menucascade>
            <uicontrol>Window</uicontrol>
            <uicontrol>Show View</uicontrol>
            <uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol>
          </menucascade>.</li>
        <li><menucascade>
            <uicontrol>Tools</uicontrol>
            <uicontrol>Git Client</uicontrol>
          </menucascade>.</li>
        <li><menucascade>
            <uicontrol conref="../add-ons/sa-toolbar-git.dita#sa-toolbar-git/sa-toolbar-git"/>
            <uicontrol
              conref="git-toolbar-shared.dita#git-toolbar-shared/sa-toolbar-git-show-staging"/>
          </menucascade>
        </li>
      </ul></section>
    <p><fig id="fig_tlr_p45_nsb">
        <title>Git Staging view</title>
        <image href="img/staging/staging_view.png" placement="inline"
          id="image_m3r_f5k_gjc"/>
      </fig></p>
    <section id="section_git_staging_view_toolbar"><title>Git Staging Toolbar </title><p
        id="p_git_staging_toolbar_intro">The toolbar contains the main repository-level
        actions.</p><p>On the <uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs0-git-staging-view"/>
        toolbar, <uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs1-git-staging-push"/>,
          <uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs2-git-staging-pull"/>, or
            <uicontrol><image href="../img/Stash18.png" id="image_qp1_1mp_pjc"/>Stash</uicontrol>
        changes to perform repository control. Select
          <?oxy_comment_start author="adrian_lapadat" timestamp="20260617T024340+0300" comment="fix ui casing difference this is outrageous haha
"?><uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs4-git-staging-open-history"/>
        or <uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs5-git-staging-open-branch-manager"
        /><?oxy_comment_end?> to view the repository history and manage branches. </p><p
        id="section_git_staging_ellipsis_menu">The <uicontrol><image href="img/icons/Ellipsis18.png"
            id="image_ijt_5qq_pjc"/>Vertical Ellipsis</uicontrol> menu provides access to repository setup,
        synchronization, configuration, and credentialing actions. For a full list of commands available from the <uicontrol>Git Staging</uicontrol> view and related locations, see <xref
          href="git-addon-actions-reference.dita#git-addon-actions-reference"/> and <xref
          href="git-addon-git-menu.dita#git-addon-git-menu"/>.</p><p><fig id="fig_etq_fzq_pjc">
          <title>Git Staging toolbar</title>
          <image href="img/staging/git-staging-toolbar.png" id="image_sxm_hzq_pjc"/>
        </fig></p></section>
    <section id="section_ych_stq_pjc"><title>Git Staging Header</title><p>The header contains
        working copy and branch actions.<ul id="ul_nyd_ztq_pjc">
          <li>On <uicontrol>Working copy</uicontrol>, switch to an existing working copy or add a
            new one.</li>
          <li>On <uicontrol>Branch</uicontrol>, switch to an existing local branch. </li>
        </ul></p><p><fig id="fig_nrm_r5q_pjc">
          <title>Git Staging header</title>
          <image href="img/staging/git-staging-header.png" id="image_o1d_55q_pjc"/>
        </fig></p></section>
    <section id="section_dzh_t2q_pjc"><title>Git Staging File Areas</title><p
        id="p_git_staging_file_context_menu_intro">Use the file areas to keep track of which changes
        are staged.</p><p><ul id="ul_gxc_vfq_pjc">
          <li id="li_rcg_nr5_nsb"><uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol>: lists modified files that
            are not staged.</li>
          <li id="li_tmw_vr5_nsb"><uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol>: lists files that are ready to
            be committed.</li>
        </ul></p><p><fig id="fig_bw3_ddr_pjc">
          <title>Git Staging file areas</title>
          <image href="img/staging/git-staging-file-areas.png" id="image_chk_gdr_pjc"/>
        </fig></p></section>
    <section id="section_qpm_dfr_pjc"><title>File Area Actions</title><p>Right-click an unstaged or
        staged file to access the following actions:</p><p><table frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1"
          id="table_bds_dfr_pjc">
          <title>Git Staging file area actions</title>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="2*"/>
            <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="5*"/>
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry>Action</entry>
                <entry>Description</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_open_in_compare_editor"
                      ><uicontrol>Open in Compare Editor</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Opens a comparison for the selected changed file so you can review the exact
                  edits before staging or committing it. Also triggered by double-clicking a file in
                  the <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_open"
                      ><uicontrol>Open</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Opens the selected file, folder, or submodule in the editor view.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><uicontrol>Show in Explorer</uicontrol></entry>
                <entry>Shows the resource in File Explorer.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_stage"
                      ><uicontrol>Stage</uicontrol></xref>
                </entry>
                <entry>Moves the resource to the <uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol> area. Available
                  for unstaged files.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><uicontrol>Unstage</uicontrol></entry>
                <entry>Moves the resource to the <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area.
                  Available for staged files.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><uicontrol
                    conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/git-client-conflicts-resolve-conflict"
                  /></entry>
                <entry>Opens a submenu with conflict resolution actions. Available for conflicted
                  files.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_discard"
                      ><uicontrol>Discard</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Discards a selected file's unstaged changes and replaces them with the last
                  committed version. Does not discard staged changes.</entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table></p><p>Staged files show additional actions:</p><ul id="ul_cds_dfr_pjc">
        <li><xref
            href="git-addon-actions-branches-history.dita#git-addon-actions-branches-history/action_show_history"
              ><uicontrol>Show History</uicontrol></xref> - Opens the commit history for the
          selected file in the <uicontrol>Git History</uicontrol> view.</li>
        <li><xref
            href="git-addon-actions-branches-history.dita#git-addon-actions-branches-history/action_show_blame"
              ><uicontrol>Show Blame</uicontrol></xref> - Opens the file in the editor and colors
          each line based on the commit that last modified it.</li>
      </ul></section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_conflict_actions"><title>Conflict Resolution
        Actions</title><p>The following actions are available during an in-progress operation such
        as an interrupted merge or rebase. To use them, right-click a conflicted file, select
        <uicontrol conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/git-client-conflicts-resolve-conflict"/>, and choose one of the following actions: See <xref
          href="git-addon-resolve-file-conflicts.dita#git-addon-resolve-file-conflicts"
          />.</p><p><table frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1" id="table_git_staging_conflict_actions">
          <title>Git Staging conflict resolution actions</title>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="2*"/>
            <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="5*"/>
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry>Action</entry>
                <entry>Description</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_resolve_using_mine"
                      ><uicontrol>Resolve Using Mine</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Resolves a conflicted file by keeping the local version and discarding the
                  incoming version.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_resolve_using_theirs"
                      ><uicontrol>Resolve Using Theirs</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Resolves a conflicted file by keeping the incoming version and discarding the
                  local version.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_resolve_with_ai"
                      ><uicontrol>Resolve with AI</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Uses the <ph keyref="plugin-positron"/> assistant to analyze a conflicted
                  file and propose a resolution. See <xref
                    href="git-addon-ai-assisted-conflict-resolution.dita#git-addon-ai-assisted-conflict-resolution"
                  />.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_mark_as_resolved"
                      ><uicontrol>Mark as Resolved</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Marks a conflicted file as resolved after you edit it and choose which
                  changes to keep.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_abort_operation"
                      ><uicontrol>Abort</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Stops the current in-progress operation and restores the repository to its
                  state before the operation started.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_restart_merge"
                      ><uicontrol>Restart Merge</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Restarts the current merge so you can resolve conflicts again from the
                  beginning.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts.dita#git-addon-actions-synchronize-conflicts/action_continue_rebase"
                      ><uicontrol>Continue Rebase</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Continues the current rebase after conflicts are resolved.</entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table></p></section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_file_areas"><title>Stage Actions</title><p
        id="p_git_staging_file_areas_intro">The stage actions are located on <uicontrol
          conref="git-staging-uicontrols.dita#git-staging-uicontrols/gs0-git-staging-view"/> between
        the <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> and <uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol>
          areas.</p><p><table frame="all" rowsep="1" colsep="1"
          id="table_git_staging_stage_controls">
          <title>Stage controls</title>
          <tgroup cols="2">
            <colspec colname="c1" colwidth="2*"/>
            <colspec colname="c2" colwidth="5*"/>
            <thead>
              <row>
                <entry>Action</entry>
                <entry>Description</entry>
              </row>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_stage_selected"
                      ><uicontrol>Stage Selected</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Moves the selected unstaged files to the <uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol>
                  area.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_stage_all"
                      ><uicontrol>Stage All</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Moves all unstaged files to the <uicontrol>Staged files</uicontrol> area. Use
                  only when all current changes belong in the same commit.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_unstage_selected"
                      ><uicontrol>Unstage Selected</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Moves the selected staged files back to the <uicontrol>Unstaged
                    files</uicontrol> area without reverting local changes.</entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry><xref
                    href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_unstage_all"
                      ><uicontrol>Unstage All</uicontrol></xref></entry>
                <entry>Moves all staged files back to the <uicontrol>Unstaged files</uicontrol> area
                  without removing local changes.</entry>
              </row>
            </tbody>
          </tgroup>
        </table></p><p><fig id="fig_y4x_ngr_pjc">
          <title>Stage actions</title>
          <image href="img/staging/staging-controls--hl.png" id="image_z4x_ngr_pjc"/>
        </fig></p></section>
    <section id="section_git_staging_commit_area"><title>Commit actions</title><p>On
          <uicontrol>Commit message</uicontrol>, enter a message that describes the staged changes.
        Then, <uicontrol>Commit</uicontrol> them to the current local branch. </p><p>For more
        information, see <xref href="git-addon-committing.dita#git-addon-committing"
      />.</p></section>
    <section id="section_zpp_x4q_pjc"><title>Commit message actions</title><p>The commit message
        toolbar includes actions that modify the commit and commit message:</p><p>The following
        actions modify the commit message:</p><ul id="ul_ksx_jrq_pjc">
        <li><xref
            href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_generate_commit_message_ai"
              ><uicontrol>Generate Commit Message Using AI</uicontrol></xref> uses the <ph
            keyref="plugin-positron"/> assistant to generate a commit message for the staged
          changes.</li>
        <li><xref
            href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_choose_previous_comment"
              ><uicontrol>Choose a Previously Used Comment</uicontrol></xref> lets you reuse a
          previous commit message.</li>
      </ul><p>The following actions modify commit behavior:</p><ul id="ul_lsx_jrq_pjc">
        <li><xref
            href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_auto_push_after_commit"
              ><uicontrol>Automatically Push Changes to Remote Branch</uicontrol></xref> pushes the
          committed changes to the remote repository immediately after committing.</li>
        <li><xref
            href="git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit.dita#git-addon-actions-review-stage-commit/action_amend_last_commit"
              ><uicontrol>Amend Last Commit</uicontrol></xref> combines staged changes with the most
          recent commit or edits the last commit message. Do not amend commits already pushed to a
          shared remote branch. </li>
      </ul><p><fig id="fig_c2j_5cr_pjc">
          <title><uicontrol>Commit message</uicontrol> actions</title>
          <image href="img/staging/commit-controls--hl.png" id="image_d2j_5cr_pjc"/>
        </fig></p></section>
  </body>
</topic>